      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Snapshot is an open-source checkpoint and restore system for GPU workloads on Kubernetes that captures fully initialized CPU and GPU memory state.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Benchmark results on NVIDIA B200 GPUs with VAST NFS storage show that restoring GPU state dominates large restores at 18 to 29 seconds, while CRIU-based CPU process restore takes 4.2 to 10.8 seconds.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Snapshot , a new open-source component of the NVIDIA DSX AI Factory Platform , makes initialized GPU workloads reusable across inference replicas—speeding startup and recovery.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Crusoe , an upstream contributor to Snapshot, reduced GLM-5.3 Pod readiness time from roughly 8 minutes to 31 seconds on NVIDIA HGX B300.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Saturn Cloud , a token factory platform, benchmarked NVIDIA Snapshot for scale-from-zero inference, cutting vLLM startup from 2–8.5 minutes to 6–34 seconds on NVIDIA HGX B300 .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Across all tested configurations, Snapshot brings a replica back in under 45 seconds, 8x to 36x faster than a cold start.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Restore times stayed under 43 seconds: Across all tested configurations, Snapshot restored replicas in 3.6 to 42.7 seconds—8x to 36x faster than cold start.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Moving GPU state dominates large restores: For the eight-GPU MoE configurations, restoring GPU state took 18 to 29 seconds.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/start-and-restore-gpu-workloads-in-seconds-with-nvidia-snapshot/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:44.200Z"
